@time 2026-11-20T14:27:19-05:00
@tokenUsage 137541 / 1097 / $0.572104
@model open-router/anthropic/claude-opus-5.5
> assistant
Your example confirms the whitespace case. The last cell starts with `, "/**`, so the space before the opening quote makes the quoted branch fail. The fallback then splits the cell at `processes,`.

You didn't pick an option for question 2, so I went with option a, the simpler one. Spaces and tabs before the opening quote and after the closing quote are now part of the quoted column and get the column color. Unquoted cells work the same as before. Multi-line quoted values are still colored one line at a time.

